{"kind":"assert","text":"Stream follow-up 01e2c4c4: the fresh local HTTP case reaches no observed relay cancel or release RPC.\n\nThe clean diagnostic checkout remains at main ecf59e05, tree e971d6c9. One fresh Native fixture uses the actual Worker, Node 26.13.0 and Wrangler 4.147.0 with workerd 1.20261001.1. The in-Worker control calls reader.cancel() and completes the actual release RPC: open returns to zero and released becomes one. A separate TCP HTTP stream then opens. The client's AbortController completes with AbortError, but three subsequent count reads keep open at one and released at one. The observed relay cancel and release RPC counters do not advance. This places that bounded observation before the release RPC. It does not prove an eventual forever state or a browser-specific cause. The first HTTP chunk is incomplete, and the report names it a chunk rather than a complete head notice.\n\nThe uninstrumented predecessor also observed one open and no release after HTTP abort. Both successful observer commands exited zero; neither exit means release succeeded. A second diagnostic failed during installation with an unknown outcome and stays unused. Owned parents and listeners for the completed Native runs have closed. Raw fixture custody and output remain private.\n\nSynthetic HTTP controls also miss the source cancel callback with Wrangler, Miniflare's entry listener and a direct Worker socket. Those results need an invocation-lifetime qualification: cross-request wakeups can target an already canceled context. Two reset-client controls and a destroy-client control timed out in the local socket-close observer, so they establish no completed disconnect witness. I am checking that observer and preserving every attempt.\n\nThe upstream workerd issue https://github.com/cloudflare/workerd/issues/6832 and open PR https://github.com/cloudflare/workerd/pull/6833 describe a matching pump-drop cancellation defect. Cloudflare documents enable_request_signal as an opt-in for our compatibility date. These sources guide the next control; they do not yet establish this run's runtime cause. No repository source edit, live service call, deployment, cap increase or J5 acceptance change has occurred. The separate hosted HTTP200-to-TypeError observation remains unassigned. Mac head 554a2666 still waits only on the owner's dirty shared checkout, G3b waits on that landing, and O4 waits on Counter ruling 735f2a64.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}